  ('90d58a66-b206-52c8-af6d-0470a9b0175c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'integers-rational-numbers'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What is the distance between the points $(3, -4)$ and $(3, 6)$ on a coordinate plane?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$2$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-absolute-values-across-zero"},{"text":"$10$ units","is_correct":true},{"text":"$16$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-every-coordinate"},{"text":"$0$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-the-x-coordinates"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$10$ units$q$, $q$The points share the $x$-coordinate $3$, so they lie on a vertical line. One point is $|-4| = 4$ units below the $x$-axis and the other is $|6| = 6$ units above it. They are on opposite sides, so add: $4 + 6 = 10$ units. The choice $2$ units subtracts $6 - 4$, which only works when both points are on the same side.$q$, 'draft', null)
