  ('dfe9c93c-7061-5833-a7c8-5253715f6e5c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'integers-rational-numbers'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What is the distance between the points $(-7, 2)$ and $(-1, 2)$ on a coordinate plane?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$-6$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-a-negative-distance"},{"text":"$0$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-the-y-coordinates"},{"text":"$8$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-absolute-values-on-the-same-side"},{"text":"$6$ units","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$6$ units$q$, $q$The points share the $y$-coordinate $2$, so they lie on a horizontal line. Both $x$-coordinates are negative, so both points are left of the $y$-axis, at $|-7| = 7$ and $|-1| = 1$ units. Same side, so subtract: $7 - 1 = 6$ units. The choice $8$ units adds the distances, which only works when the points are on opposite sides. A distance is never negative, so $-6$ units is not possible.$q$, 'draft', null)
