   $q$Which statement explains why $-3 > -8$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$-3$ is to the left of $-8$ on a number line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-number-line-direction"},{"text":"$-3$ is farther from $0$ than $-8$ is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-greater-with-farther-from-zero"},{"text":"$-3$ is to the right of $-8$ on a number line.","is_correct":true},{"text":"$-3$ and $-8$ are equal because both are negative.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-all-negatives-are-equal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-3$ is to the right of $-8$ on a number line.$q$, $q$On a horizontal number line, values increase to the right. $-3$ is to the right of $-8$, so $-3 > -8$. The statement that $-3$ is farther from $0$ is false: $-3$ is $3$ units from $0$ and $-8$ is $8$ units from $0$.$q$, 'draft', null)
