  ('df1b27a9-1af3-550c-9c71-47eaf4f15641', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'integers-rational-numbers'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which number has the greatest absolute value: $-\frac{3}{4}$, $\frac{2}{3}$, $-\frac{1}{2}$ or $\frac{5}{8}$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{2}{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-the-greatest-value"},{"text":"$\\frac{5}{8}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compared-fraction-digits-as-whole-numbers"},{"text":"$-\\frac{3}{4}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$-\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-the-greatest-negative"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-\frac{3}{4}$$q$, $q$The absolute values are $\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$, $\frac{2}{3} \approx 0.67$, $\frac{1}{2} = 0.5$ and $\frac{5}{8} = 0.625$. The greatest is $0.75$, so the answer is $-\frac{3}{4}$. The choice $\frac{2}{3}$ is the greatest number in the list, but $-\frac{3}{4}$ is farther from $0$.$q$, 'draft', null)
