   $q$A rectangle on a coordinate plane has vertices at $(-4, 3)$, $(2, 3)$, $(2, -1)$ and $(-4, -1)$. What is the perimeter of the rectangle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$8$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-absolute-values-across-zero"},{"text":"$10$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-only-two-sides"},{"text":"$24$ units","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-area-instead-of-perimeter"},{"text":"$20$ units","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$20$ units$q$, $q$The top side runs from $x = -4$ to $x = 2$. These are on opposite sides of the $y$-axis, so its length is $4 + 2 = 6$ units. The right side runs from $y = 3$ to $y = -1$, so its length is $3 + 1 = 4$ units. The perimeter is $6 + 4 + 6 + 4 = 20$ units. The choice $24$ units multiplies $6 \times 4$, which is the area.$q$, 'draft', null)
