   $q$A gym charges a 20 dollar joining fee plus 15 dollars per month. Which statement about the total cost and the number of months is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is proportional, with a constant of proportionality of 35.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-fee-to-rate"},{"text":"It is proportional, because the cost goes up 15 dollars every month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"constant-rate-means-proportional"},{"text":"It is not proportional, because the cost for 0 months would be 20 dollars, not 0.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is not proportional, because the cost keeps increasing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"increasing-means-not-proportional"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is not proportional, because the cost for 0 months would be 20 dollars, not 0.$q$, $q$The cost is $c = 15m + 20$. For 1 month the ratio is $\frac{35}{1} = 35$ and for 2 months it is $\frac{50}{2} = 25$, so the ratio is not constant, and at 0 months the cost is 20 dollars. Rising by the same amount each month is not enough when there is a starting fee.$q$, 'draft', null)
