   $q$Pump A moves water according to $y = 7.5x$, where $y$ is gallons and $x$ is minutes. A table for Pump B shows $34$ gallons in $4$ minutes and $85$ gallons in $10$ minutes, and it is also proportional. How many more gallons does Pump B move than Pump A in $12$ minutes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-difference-in-unit-rates"},{"text":"$102$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-pump-b-total-only"},{"text":"$12$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$90$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-pump-a-total-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$12$$q$, $q$Pump B's constant is $\frac{34}{4} = \frac{85}{10} = 8.5$ gallons per minute. In 12 minutes, Pump B moves $8.5 \times 12 = 102$ gallons and Pump A moves $7.5 \times 12 = 90$ gallons, so the difference is $102 - 90 = 12$. The choice $1$ is the difference per minute, not over 12 minutes.$q$, 'draft', null)
